  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": "<p>For a Fedora3 RELS-EXT datastream that was identified as \"RELS-EXT.1\" in the foxml, even though there was only one version of the RELS-EXT content, the migration tool put RELS-EXT in OCFL v2, instead of v1 with the other datastreams. There's only one version of the RELS-EXT, so it can just be in OCFL v1.</p>\n\n<p>Here's the relevant foxml:</p>\n\n<p>&lt;foxml:datastream ID=\"RELS-EXT\" STATE=\"A\" CONTROL_GROUP=\"X\" VERSIONABLE=\"true\"&gt;<br/>\n      &lt;foxml:datastreamVersion ID=\"RELS-EXT.1\" LABEL=\"External Relations\" CREATED=\"2019-05-09T15:52:01.885Z\" MIMETYPE=\"application/rdf+xml\" FORMAT_URI=\"info:fedora/fedora-system:FedoraRELSExt-1.0\" SIZE=\"318\"&gt;<br/>\n                &lt;foxml:contentDigest TYPE=\"MD5\" DIGEST=\"870c9172498c0459d45df88b9686c8e8\"/&gt;<br/>\n                &lt;foxml:xmlContent&gt;<br/>\n&lt;rdf:RDF xmlns:fedora-model=\"info:fedora/fedora-system:def/model#\" xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\"&gt;<br/>\n &lt;rdf:Description rdf:about=\"info:fedora/test:233605\"&gt;<br/>\n &lt;fedora-model:hasModel rdf:resource=\"info:fedora/bdr-cmodel:commonMetadata\"&gt;&lt;/fedora-model:hasModel&gt;<br/>\n &lt;/rdf:Description&gt;<br/>\n&lt;/rdf:RDF&gt;<br/>\n               &lt;/foxml:xmlContent&gt;<br/>\n       &lt;/foxml:datastreamVersion&gt;<br/>\n&lt;/foxml:datastream&gt;</p>",
